What is the final value of a after the loops are executed in the following Java program?

```java
public class Main {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int a = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
            a++;
        }

        for (int j = 0; j < 5; j++) {
            a--;
        }

        System.out.println("Final value of a: " + a);
    }
}
```

What is the final value of `a` after the loops are executed?
